{"name":"Pea Aubergine","hex":"#7c9865","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Peranakan Indonesian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain plants of the family Fabaceae: Pisum sativum and others.","A plant, Pisum sativum, member of the legume (Fabaceae) family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pea"},{"term":"aubergine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Asian plant, Solanum melongena, cultivated for its edible purple, green, or white ovoid fruit; eggplant.","The fruit of this plant, eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aubergine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Solanum torvum","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum torvum, also known as pendejera, turkey berry, devil's fig, pea eggplant, platebrush or susumber, is a bushy, erect and spiny perennial plant used horticulturally as a rootstock for eggplant. Grafted plants are very vigorous and tolerate diseases affecting the root system, thus allowing the crop to continue for a second year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_173035.jpg/330px-Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_173035.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanum_torvum","wikidata":"Q978609"},{"title":"Pea","blocks":[{"text":"Pea is a pulse or fodder crop, but the word often refers to the seed or sometimes the pod of this flowering plant species. Peas are eaten as a vegetable. The pea is native to the Mediterranean region and southwest Asia, and cultivated nearly worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Doperwt_rijserwt_peulen_Pisum_sativum.jpg/330px-Doperwt_rijserwt_peulen_Pisum_sativum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pea","wikidata":"Q25237"},{"title":"Eggplant","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum melongena is a plant species in the nightshade family Solanaceae, grown worldwide for its edible fruit, typically used as a vegetable in cooking. It is known by a number of names, including eggplant, aubergine, and brinjal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG/330px-Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant","wikidata":"Q7540"},{"title":"Eggplant (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Eggplant is a dark purple or brownish-purple color that resembles the color of the outer skin of European eggplants. Another name for the color eggplant is aubergine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Aubergine.jpg/330px-Aubergine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant_(color)","wikidata":"Q1403218"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg/500px-Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg/1280px-Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg/500px-Solanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foliage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolanum_torvum_at_Kampung_Bukit_Jagong_20230629_172945.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.